$$
\begin{aligned}
1:&\quad\mathrm{HL+HCO_3^-\rightleftharpoons H_2CO_3+L^-}:&&K_1,\\
2:&\quad\mathrm{HL+H_2O\rightleftharpoons H_3O^++L^-}:&&K_2=K_{\mathrm{HL}},\\
3:&\quad\mathrm{HCO_3^-+H_3O^+\rightleftharpoons H_2CO_3+H_2O}:&&K_3=\frac1{K_{a1}}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Reaction 1 = 2 + 3, $K_1=K_2\cdot K_3=311\quad(3.1\times10^2)$.

Alternative:

$$
K_1=\frac{[\mathrm{H_2CO_3}][\mathrm{L^-}]}{[\mathrm{HL}][\mathrm{HCO_3^-}]}
\times\frac{[\mathrm{H_3O^+}]}{[\mathrm{H_3O^+}]}
=\frac{[\mathrm{H_3O^+}][\mathrm{L^-}]}{[\mathrm{HL}]}
\times\frac{[\mathrm{H_2CO_3}]}{[\mathrm{HCO_3^-}][\mathrm{H_3O^+}]}.
$$

A: $\mathrm{pH}=7.40$; $[\mathrm{H_3O^+}]=4.0\times10^{-8}$; $[\mathrm{HCO_3^-}]_A=0.022$.

From $K_{a1}$: $[\mathrm{H_2CO_3}]_A=0.0019$;

$$
[\mathrm{HCO_3^-}]_B+[\mathrm{H_2CO_3}]_B=0.0239\quad(0.024).\tag{1}
$$

B: $\mathrm{pH}=7.00$;

$$
\frac{[\mathrm{HCO_3^-}]}{[\mathrm{H_2CO_3}]}=4.5;
$$

$$
[\mathrm{HCO_3^-}]_B=4.5[\mathrm{H_2CO_3}]_B.\tag{2}
$$

From (1) and (2): $[\mathrm{HCO_3^-}]_B=0.0196$, $[\mathrm{H_2CO_3}]_B=0.0043$.

$$
n(\mathrm{HL})=\Delta n(\mathrm{H_2CO_3})=\Delta c(\mathrm{H_2CO_3})\times1.00\ \mathrm{dm}^3=2.4\times10^{-3}\ \mathrm{mol}.
$$
